  ('ent_yuri-gagarin', 'person', 'yuri-gagarin', 'Yuri Gagarin', 'published', 'Yuri Alekseyevich Gagarin (9 March 1934 – 27 March 1968) was a Soviet pilot and cosmonaut who became the first person to journey into outer space during the first successful crewed spaceflight. He was launched from the Baikonur Cosmodrome in the Kazakh SSR. Travelling on Vostok 1, Gagarin completed one orbit of Earth on 12 April 1961. The flight took 108 minutes. By achieving this major milestone ', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

